s are labeled below.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### Exam information\n\n- **When:** Wednesday of Week 6 during class time.\n- **Where:** Our usual classroom.\n- **Duration:** 50 minutes.\n- **Resources:** You are not allowed to use any resource (calculator, notes, etc.) for the exam. Bring a pencil and an eraser.\n- **Sections covered:** 6.1–6.4.\n\n### Question formats\n\nThe exam will have two classes of problems:\n\n- Multiple-choice, choose many, true/false, fill-in-the-blank, and matching problems. For most of these problems you do not receive partial credit.\n- Show-your-work problems. These are similar to the ones appearing on written homework in terms of appearance and difficulty. You receive partial credit for partial progress toward the answer on these problems.\n\n### Preparation advice\n\n- Look back to what you’ve done in class:\n  - Review problems in Achieve.\n  - Revisit the written homework problems (and keys).\n  - Revisit the recitation worksheets (and keys).\n- Look at the exercises at the end of each section in the textbook.\n- Look at the review exercises at the end of each chapter in the textbook.\n\n### Topic list\n\nThe source states: **This is NOT a comprehensive list of topics appearing on the exam.**\n\n| Source section | Study objectives |\n| --- | --- |\n| Section 6.1: Vector Fields | 1–6 |\n| Section 6.2: Line Integrals | 7–10 |\n| Section 6.3: Conservative Vector Fields | 11–14 |\n| Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem | 15–21 |" :tutorial/id #uuid "e00680d4-65b3-54a6-bdeb-532960b5e38b" :tutorial/title "Exam information and preparation advice"}] [:question/id #uuid "831437ec-331e-588a-a4fc-f9926b919479" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748470 :question/id #uuid "831437ec-331e-588a-a4fc-f9926b919479" :question/problem "Source study objective: (2), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nUnderstand and identify conservative vector fields."}] [:question/id #uuid "8bdf637d-b6aa-5004-af9c-968338e54de3" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748472 :question/id #uuid "8bdf637d-b6aa-5004-af9c-968338e54de3" :question/problem "Source study objective: (3), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nFind the gradient field of a scalar function."}] [:question/id #uuid "94603b3c-468a-5ad9-aa53-bc95c311b2c3" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748474 :question/id #uuid "94603b3c-468a-5ad9-aa53-bc95c311b2c3" :question/problem "Source study objective: (15), PDF page 2. Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem.\n\nApply Green’s Theorem to evaluate line integrals along closed, positively oriented curves in the plane."}] [:question/id #uuid "9772078f-e71d-56ac-9f1e-9d63ec921ab4" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748476 :question/id #uuid "9772078f-e71d-56ac-9f1e-9d63ec921ab4" :question/problem "Source study objective: (6), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nFor a conservative field, understand the relation between its equipotential curves and streamlines."}] [:question/id #uuid "ab4b8394-b25e-5685-b651-2f397faeacbd" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748479 :question/id #uuid "ab4b8394-b25e-5685-b651-2f397faeacbd" :question/problem "Source study objective: (14), PDF page 2. Section 6.3: Conservative Vector Fields.\n\nUnderstand the concept of path independence and its relationship to closed loops."}] [:question/id #uuid "c391c684-d869-5113-80bb-81d9755987d9" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748485 :question/id #uuid "c391c684-d869-5113-80bb-81d9755987d9" :question/problem "Source study objective: (17), PDF page 2. Section 6.4: Green’s Theorem.\n\nDistinguish between the circulation form and the flux form of Green’s Theorem."}] [:question/id #uuid "d4e361c4-2176-5bb1-b2cb-b120dad34adf" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748488 :question/id #uuid "d4e361c4-2176-5bb1-b2cb-b120dad34adf" :question/problem "Source study objective: (1), PDF page 2. Section 6.1: Vector Fields.\n\nSketch or identify a vector field given its algebraic formula."}] [:question/id #uuid "d9026202-4ba6-5ebd-a2c6-47817a4d77d0" {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186748489 :question/id #uuid "d9026202-4ba6-5ebd-a2c6-47817a4d77d0" :question/pro